// The noisy face of mn-hof-row-gate: a param typed `() -> Int with !WASI`
// receives a thunk that PRINTS. The negation row judges the argument edge
// and reports one E_EffectMismatch — and since 2026-09-25 the class is
// ARMED, so the report is a refusal: no WAT, nonzero exit. This fixture
// used to live inside mn-hof-row-gate.mn beside the quiet face, banked as
// "exit 42 with exactly one E_EffectMismatch" — a real `!WASI` leak that
// the era's unarmed class let run (§9.11: a banked expectation is a
// hypothesis about the era that banked it).
// Expected: REFUSE with exactly one E_EffectMismatch (the noisy edge).

fn noisy() = {
  println("boom")
  42
}

fn accept_thunk(f: () -> Int with !WASI) -> Int with !WASI = f()

fn main() = accept_thunk(noisy)
